## Priority 1: Split Query Strategy + AsNoTracking()

### Problem: Cartesian Product Explosion

**Symptoms:**
- Single query with 10+ `Include()` statements
- Multiple `ThenInclude()` chains
- Query returns massive result sets
- Memory consumption spikes
- Execution time increases exponentially with data size

**Root Cause:**
When EF Core loads multiple collections in one query, it creates a Cartesian product. Example:
- 10 FundingPartners × 5 ClientPartners × 20 Stakeholders = 1,000 rows for 1 entity!
- With more collections, this explodes: 10 × 5 × 20 × 15 × 8 = 60,000+ rows!

### Solution Pattern

**❌ BEFORE (Anti-Pattern):**
```csharp
public async Task<SomeModel> GetDetailedDataAsync(int id)
{
    var entity = await context.Set<Entity>()
        .Include(e => e.Collection1).ThenInclude(c1 => c1.Related1)
        .Include(e => e.Collection1).ThenInclude(c1 => c1.Related2)
        .Include(e => e.Collection2).ThenInclude(c2 => c2.Related1)
        .Include(e => e.Collection3).ThenInclude(c3 => c3.Related1)
        .Include(e => e.Collection4).ThenInclude(c4 => c4.Related1)
        .Include(e => e.Collection5).ThenInclude(c5 => c5.Related1)
        .Include(e => e.SimpleNavigation1)
        .Include(e => e.SimpleNavigation2)
        // ... more includes creating Cartesian explosion
        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(e => e.Id == id);
    
    if (entity == null)
        throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Entity with ID {id} not found");
    
    // Process entity...
    return MapToModel(entity);
}
```

**✅ AFTER (Optimized Pattern):**
```csharp
public async Task<SomeModel> GetDetailedDataAsync(int id)
{
    // ==========================================
    // QUERY 1: Main entity with SIMPLE navigation properties only
    // ==========================================
    var entity = await context.Set<Entity>()
        .AsNoTracking() // ✅ No change tracking for read-only operation
        .Include(e => e.SimpleNavigation1)
        .Include(e => e.SimpleNavigation2)
        .Include(e => e.SimpleNavigation3)
        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(e => e.Id == id);
    
    if (entity == null)
        throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Entity with ID {id} not found");
    
    // ==========================================
    // QUERY 2-N: Load each COLLECTION independently
    // ==========================================
    var collection1 = await context.Set<Collection1Entity>()
        .AsNoTracking()
        .Where(c => c.EntityId == id)
        .Include(c => c.Related1)
        .Include(c => c.Related2)
        .ToListAsync();
    
    var collection2 = await context.Set<Collection2Entity>()
        .AsNoTracking()
        .Where(c => c.EntityId == id)
        .Include(c => c.Related1)
        .ToListAsync();
    
    var collection3 = await context.Set<Collection3Entity>()
        .AsNoTracking()
        .Where(c => c.EntityId == id)
        .Include(c => c.Related1)
        .ToListAsync();
    
    // Assign collections back to entity (if needed for processing)
    entity.Collection1 = collection1;
    entity.Collection2 = collection2;
    entity.Collection3 = collection3;
    
    // Process entity...
    return MapToModel(entity);
}
```

### Key Rules for Split Queries

1. **Load main entity first** with ONLY simple navigation properties (1:1 or N:1 relationships)
2. **Load each collection separately** in independent queries
3. **Always use `.AsNoTracking()`** for read-only operations
4. **Filter collections by parent ID** using `.Where(c => c.ParentId == id)`
5. **Include related data in each query** as needed
6. **Assign collections back** to parent entity if needed for processing logic

