## Priority 3: Batch Queries to Eliminate N+1 Problems

### Problem: N+1 Query Anti-Pattern

**Symptoms:**
- Queries inside loops
- One query per collection item
- Execution time scales linearly with collection size
- Database logs show many similar queries

**Example N+1 Problem:**
```csharp
// 1 query to get partners
var partners = await context.Partners.Where(p => p.Active).ToListAsync();

// N queries (one per partner) - ANTI-PATTERN!
foreach (var partner in partners)
{
    var agreements = await LoadPartnerAgreementsAsync(partner.Id); // ❌ Database call in loop
}
```

### Solution Pattern

**❌ BEFORE (N+1 Anti-Pattern):**
```csharp
var partnerSummaries = new List<string>();
foreach (var partner in partners.Take(10))
{
    // ❌ Separate query for EACH partner
    var agreements = await context.Agreements
        .Where(a => a.PartnerId == partner.Id)
        .ToListAsync();
    
    // ❌ Another query for EACH partner
    var contacts = await context.Contacts
        .Where(c => c.PartnerId == partner.Id)
        .ToListAsync();
    
    partnerSummaries.Add($"{partner.Name}: {agreements.Count} agreements, {contacts.Count} contacts");
}
// Total: 1 + (10 × 2) = 21 queries!
```

**✅ AFTER (Batched Queries):**
```csharp
var partnerSummaries = new List<string>();

// Get all partner IDs upfront
var partnerIds = partners.Take(10).Select(p => p.Id).ToList();

// ✅ BATCH QUERY 1: Load ALL agreements for ALL partners in ONE query
var allAgreements = await context.Agreements
    .AsNoTracking()
    .Where(a => partnerIds.Contains(a.PartnerId))
    .ToListAsync();

// ✅ BATCH QUERY 2: Load ALL contacts for ALL partners in ONE query
var allContacts = await context.Contacts
    .AsNoTracking()
    .Where(c => partnerIds.Contains(c.PartnerId))
    .ToListAsync();

// Group by partner for in-memory processing
var agreementsByPartner = allAgreements.GroupBy(a => a.PartnerId).ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => g.ToList());
var contactsByPartner = allContacts.GroupBy(c => c.PartnerId).ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => g.ToList());

// Process in-memory (no more database calls)
foreach (var partner in partners.Take(10))
{
    var agreements = agreementsByPartner.TryGetValue(partner.Id, out var partnerAgreements) 
        ? partnerAgreements : new List<Agreement>();
    var contacts = contactsByPartner.TryGetValue(partner.Id, out var partnerContacts) 
        ? partnerContacts : new List<Contact>();
    
    partnerSummaries.Add($"{partner.Name}: {agreements.Count} agreements, {contacts.Count} contacts");
}
// Total: 1 + 2 = 3 queries! (7x reduction)
```

### Batch Query Pattern Template

```csharp
// Step 1: Get all IDs to query
var ids = collection.Select(item => item.Id).ToList();

// Step 2: Load ALL related data in ONE query using .Contains()
var allRelatedData = await context.Set<RelatedEntity>()
    .AsNoTracking()
    .Where(r => ids.Contains(r.ForeignKeyId))
    .ToListAsync();

// Step 3: Group by foreign key for fast lookup
var dataByParentId = allRelatedData
    .GroupBy(r => r.ForeignKeyId)
    .ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => g.ToList());

// Step 4: Process in-memory (no more database calls)
foreach (var item in collection)
{
    var relatedItems = dataByParentId.TryGetValue(item.Id, out var items) 
        ? items : new List<RelatedEntity>();
    // Process relatedItems...
}
```

