## Checklist: Before and After Optimization

### Before Starting Optimization
- [ ] Measure current execution time with realistic data
- [ ] Identify all `Include()` statements in queries
- [ ] Check for queries inside loops (N+1 patterns)
- [ ] Verify if change tracking is needed
- [ ] Review database query logs
- [ ] Document current memory usage

### During Optimization
- [ ] Split queries with 5+ includes into separate queries
- [ ] Add `.AsNoTracking()` to all read-only queries
- [ ] Replace query loops with batch queries using `.Contains()`
- [ ] Add DbContextFactory to constructor (if using parallel execution)
- [ ] Implement parallel execution for 5+ independent queries
- [ ] Use `await using` for DbContext disposal in parallel tasks

### After Optimization
- [ ] Measure new execution time with same data
- [ ] Verify all data is still loaded correctly
- [ ] Check for any compilation errors
- [ ] Review database query logs (should see fewer, better queries)
- [ ] Test with various data sizes
- [ ] Monitor memory usage (should be lower)
- [ ] Document performance improvement percentage

### Code Review Checklist
- [ ] All read-only queries have `.AsNoTracking()`
- [ ] No queries inside loops (N+1 eliminated)
- [ ] Collections loaded independently (no Cartesian products)
- [ ] Parallel tasks each create their own DbContext
- [ ] All DbContexts properly disposed with `await using`
- [ ] Main entity query runs first (not parallelized)
- [ ] Dependent queries run after their dependencies

